content.text:
Plain classes like `.test` aren't recognized by Tailwind's variant system — that's why `md:test` doesn't work. You have two options (per `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`):

**Option A — make it a real utility** (so `md:test` works out of the box):
```css
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```

**Option B — put the breakpoint inside the CSS itself** using `@variant`:
```css
.test {
  @variant md {
    background: red;
  }
}
```
Then use `<h3 className="test">`.

Cite: `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx` — "Adding custom utilities > Simple utilities" and "Using custom CSS > Using variants".

